      "teaser": "the client side companion app for quartermaster",
      "thumbnail": "",
      "downloads": 651,
      "favourites_count": 1,
      "description": "<h1>Check out <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://github.com/cebarks/quartermaster/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Quartermaster!</a></h1>\n<p>the client-side companion app for the Quartermaster control panel.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<h3>Currently only syncs client mods from the server to the client.</h3>\n<h4>How it works</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Fetches the mod catalog from your Quartermaster server (with ETag caching)</li>\n<li>Diffs against local state to determine what needs to be installed, updated, or removed</li>\n<li>Downloads changed mods as a batch ZIP, extracts, and verifies SHA-256 hashes</li>\n<li>Prompts for a restart if any BepInEx plugin files changed (they’re already loaded by the time Convoy runs)</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Planned Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>optional mod groups</li>\n<li>per-user mods that are managed and updated by the server, then pushed to the user</li>\n<li>server-authorative mod configs</li>\n<li>client setting backup (keybinds, graphics settings, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Feel free to open an issue on github for any bugs or feature requests!</p>\n",
      "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2806/convoy",
      "fika_compatibility": true,
      "featured": false,
      "contains_ads": false,
      "contains_ai_content": true,
      "custom_ai_disclosure": "<p>Portions of this codebase were implemented with the assistance of LLM-based tools (Claude Code). All architecture, design decisions, and direction were done by a human (Senior Product Security Engineer w/ 10+ years of coding experience), the LLM was used as an implementation aid under continuous human supervision and review.</p>\n",
